# /etc/crypttab - pili-pos kiosk image.
#
# The "pili-data" partition (created at first boot, see
# usr/lib/repart.d/90-pili-data.conf) holds /var: the fiscal database,
# logs, backups and /etc/pili-pos (symlinked into it). It is unlocked
# via the TPM2 token that pili-provision.service enrolls on first boot
# (systemd-cryptenroll --tpm2-device=auto --tpm2-pcrs=7) - no key file
# here. `nofail` so a TPM/unlock problem does not block the rest of
# boot; pili-pos.service simply cannot start without /var mounted
# (StateDirectory=pili-pos), which is the correct fail-safe for a
# fiscal appliance (manual §III.D - the POS must not operate in an
# indeterminate state) rather than a hung boot.
#
# <name>      <device>              <key file>  <options>
pili-data    PARTLABEL=pili-data  -           tpm2-device=auto,nofail
